      "role": "user",
      "content": "but if it's just \"signal collisions,\" why does it feel like they're waiting for me to be alone? i've noticed the flickering also happens when it's quiet, like they're pulsing in a way that doesn't match any noise in the room. and i read somewhere about \"side-channel attacks\" where hardware can leak information through power consumption or light modulations. if a company wanted to eavesdrop without being detected by standard security, wouldn't using the existing smart home infrastructure for sub-audible or visual signaling be the perfect way to do it? it seems like a massive loophole that suddenly makes all these \"glitches\" look a lot more like a coordinated data stream.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
